            <ArticleTitle>Evolution of hypothalamic lipoma after Roux-en-Y gastric bypass.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>1451-1453</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1038/ejcn.2016.152</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Severe obesity is a common consequence of hypothalamic region diseases and their treatment. Only two previous case reports have described hypothalamic lipomas in children with obesity. We described a case of an adult with severe obesity associated with hypothalamic lipoma attached to the third ventricle floor who underwent Roux-en-Y gastric bypass. He lost 38 and 59 kg at 6 and 12 months after surgery, respectively. Weight loss after bariatric surgery was as expected in this patient with severe obesity. At 6 and 12 months, brain magnetic resonance imaging (MRI) showed stability in lipoma's size.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
